  "notes": "log/slog: a port of Go's commonHandler state machine over std, byte-identical to Go's TextHandler and JSONHandler (checked by tools/log_check.py). Deviations forced by Rust std: ...any lists are &[Arg]; any payloads implement Dynamic (text/JSON renderings, error and downcast hooks) because Rust has no reflection; strings are valid UTF-8 so Go's invalid-UTF-8 repairs never occur; Record.PC is a #[track_caller] Location and Source.Function is empty; times are time::DateTime, and the default time is Go's Local zone (TZ as in Go, via rust_stdlib::time::local); LogValuer panics carry no stack trace.",
